				\begin{document}$$H_{1},...,H_{B}$$\end{document} built on the balanced samples are selected. The proposed algorithm works as follows:
Divide the dataset into training and testing sets.
Over/under sample the minority/majority class observations in the training data to generate a balanced training data.
Grow classification trees on each bootstrap sample taken from the balanced training data using the Random Forest algorithm, i.e., select feature randomly while splitting the nodes in each tree.
Calculate the classification error rate on out-of-bag (OOB) observations using Eqs. 1 and 2.
Arrange the tree in ascending order with respect to their error rates.
Discard trees with high error rates and finally integrate the remaining tree for the final forest.

